# A cliff with a LADDER up it, and nothing else (M17 phase 6). A fixture.
#
# Two height units in one cell -- above SOLO_RISE, above ASSISTED_RISE's slope
# allowance, and with no ramp anywhere. So the ladder is the ONLY way up, which
# is what makes this fixture able to fail: if the climb does not work, the
# validator and the body disagree and the test says which.
#
# That disagreement is exactly what M17 found: ASCENDER_CONTENTS has listed
# LADDER since M2 and the flood counted it as a way up for months while nothing
# in the game could climb one.

name = test_ladder
base_height = 0
width = 5
length = 8
tags = foot, test, ladder

